## 15. Value Scales and Salvaged-Component Comparisons

### 15.1 Stellaris and Europa Universalis IV — Ethics Axes and Policy Slots [REF:VP-SLOTS]

- **[Comparison set]** For the 10 character value slots and the organization policy slots, the comparison set is Stellaris''s ethics pairs (Authority–Equality, Exclusivity–Openness, Militarism–Pacifism, Materialism–Spiritualism/Ritual) and policy slots, together with the Central, Innovation, and Diplomacy slots of Europa Universalis 4. Source texts for both games have not yet been collected.
- **Janseon**: Only the structure of axes and slots is compared. The original games'' galactic species names, ideology group names, and unique event text are not carried over.

### 15.2 Horizon Forbidden West — Salvaged-Component Economy [REF:HFW-SALVAGE]

- **[Document: Official Introduction]** The official PlayStation introduction (viewed 2026-09-12) explains that players craft weapons, equipment, and traps from parts salvaged from machines.
- **Janseon**: Only this economic tension is borrowed. Modules salvaged from beneath Seoul attach conditionally to equipment, traps, and weapons. They do not turn the basic unit class into archers, and the original''s proper nouns and crafting recipes are not brought over.');
INSERT INTO gdd_document (id, category_id, slug, title, summary, status, sort, source_path, body_md) VALUES ('doc.Ref-Norland-Triage', 'references', 'ref-norland-triage', 'Survey Classification of the Second Comparison Target', '', 'accepted', 28, 'references/Ref-Norland-Triage.md', '# Survey Classification of the Second Comparison Target

The reference scope is fixed at two works. The first work is documented separately, and this document records the result of classifying the second comparison target across Seoul''s eighteen domains.

## Survey Status

The sealed survey ledger has classified rows for all eighteen domains. The total of 1526 rows breaks down into 1423 document-verified rows, 58 unresolved rows, 43 non-corresponding rows, and 2 conflicting rows.

This document is a classification that restates that ledger by domain. The absence of a separate survey document does not mean no survey was done. Domains that have rows are not listed as unsurveyed, and rows that are not document-verified are not promoted to verified.

## Classification by Domain

| Domain | Name in Seoul | Classified Rows | Document-Verified | Unresolved | Non-Corresponding | Conflicting | Adopted |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| D01 | Time and Calendar | 59 | 39 | 19 | 1 | 0 | None |
| D02 | Living and Consumables | 32 | 32 | 0 | 0 | 0 | None |
