## 3.1 State, Institutions, and Legitimacy

Seoul fact: State formation refers to the owner-confirmed contract in canon/contracts/state-formation-contract.json. It does not redefine independent acquisition → state transition, prior enrollment, personal holdings, or the distinction of territory. The tier, position, occupation, and command authority of SP-1.0.0 are each separate authorities. The Six-Jiri Kingdom is a non-holder, and its limited notification right is not expanded into an approval right.

## 3.2 Titles, Rights, Justification, and Ratification

Seoul fact: The settlement at https://github.com/islee23520/seoul-dengoku/blob/3e3c03349eafaaf88347d119a4bdd0c6d44abc53/GAME/Assets/Janseon/Foundation/Presentation/SeoulCampaignSession.cs#L68 is property, not a new title distribution. Ratification, support, and authority qualifications follow SP-1.0.0. CK3 reference: the contract groups and tier trees in mechanics-06-vassals-court-council.md:11-95 and depth-02-power-structures.md:178-206 are references for expressing rights. Corrected static reference — limited to the PASS scope of depth-verification-20261027.md:1855-1900; the clan multiplier and final tax rate summary are not adopted because of a verification mismatch.

## 3.3 Grants, Delegation, Revocation, and Vassal Contracts

Seoul fact: Shared affiliation alone does not create command authority or ownership. Settlement accounting does not change the ownership graph (https://github.com/islee23520/seoul-dengoku/blob/3e3c03349eafaaf88347d119a4bdd0c6d44abc53/GAME/Assets/Janseon/Core/SettlementDomain.cs#L426-L452). CK3 reference: depth-02-power-structures.md:289-295 is a case that distinguishes negotiation stages from separate checkbox-style rights. Product authority: Seoul''s policies and formulas for tribute, vassalage, delegation, revocation, and ownership transfer are institutionally undecided.

## 3.4 Council and Court Positions

CK3 reference: the position, task, and competence fields in mechanics-06-vassals-court-council.md:116-177,193-226 and the task schema in depth-02-power-structures.md:407-493 are references for separating positions from task progress. Gauge sizes and monthly increase values are not carried over. Product authority: the existence of a Seoul council, court, and regency, and their tiers of authority, are institutionally undecided.

## 3.5 Succession, Death, and Main Body Transfer

Seoul fact: The approval scope for the main body and successors follows SP-1.0.0 and the existing succession provisions. CK3 reference: mechanics-07-succession.md:11-82,144-209 and depth-02-power-structures.md:297-406 distinguish law settings, electors, candidate scores, and designated candidates. A death hook is not evidence of the moment of actual asset transfer. Product authority: Seoul''s succession, election system, and asset inheritance policies are institutionally undecided; the CK3 dynasty legacy track totals are excluded because of an independent verification mismatch.

## 3.6 State Formation and Control Boundaries

Seoul fact: Enemy control at https://github.com/islee23520/seoul-dengoku/blob/3e3c03349eafaaf88347d119a4bdd0c6d44abc53/GAME/Assets/Janseon/Core/CampaignTurnDomain.cs#L224-L226 is a faction inequality determination and does not consume alliances or treaties. Current code facts are not taken as approval of a conquest legal framework. Product authority: alliance and conquest policies refer to the same undecided ledger as CH7.

