### RSAVE-16 Battle State Continuity



## Resolution Order

1. Fix the starting values and the choice log.
2. Split random number streams into battle, encounter, and world event streams.
3. Name randomness opens only the character stream.
4. For every state change, record in the ledger the cause ID, command, world time, subject and target, before and after hashes, and rule and content versions.
5. Interviews, deals, and succession support are recorded only as character micro-lines.
6. When the sum of micro-lines exceeds the threshold, escalate it to a world event.
7. Saved content is limited to the versioned world state, command and event positions, the content version, the immutable battle context, the command log with acceptance order, and the settlement receipt.
8. Write to a temporary file and verify the checksum.
9. Swap in for the original only after verification.
10. Reject unsupported versions, truncated files, and bad checksums, and return an error.
11. Keep the previous backup.
12. Open battle saves only before the context is issued, at a checkpoint where state and accepted commands are finalized together, and after settlement is complete.
13. Reading a mid-battle save restores only the saved immutable context and the accepted battle command log.
14. Check that each unit''s logical position, facing, and current order match those from before the save.
15. Check that confirmed replacement commands after restoration are applied at the next simulation step in the same acceptance order as before the save.

## Prohibitions

- The same starting values and choice log producing a different world state
- The same log producing a different event checksum
- One system''s processing order shaking another system''s results
- Mixing random number streams
- Changing state without a ledger entry
- Finalizing with a ledger entry missing
- Escalating a character''s action to a world event before the threshold
- Using any stream other than the character stream for name randomness
- Swapping in for the original before verifying the checksum
- Silently reading an unsupported version
- Silently reading a truncated file
- Silently reading a bad checksum
- Discarding the previous backup
- Re-querying the campaign when reading a mid-battle save
- Re-rolling a unit''s logical position, facing, and current order after a save
- Turning saving into a new turn-end rule or time interval for real-time battle
- Losing the deterministic order of accepted replacement commands

## Sources

- [Save and Determinism](/gdd/rules/save-and-determinism/)
- Implementation constants take precedence over contract values
- The source text has no locked values. The table carries over only the source wording
- The threshold for a character''s micro-line is not given as a number in the source text
- The succession and name roster documents are merely where the source text points to the micro-line, and add no values to these rules');
