## 9.1 World Time and Battle Time

Seoul fact: https://github.com/islee23520/seoul-dengoku/blob/3e3c03349eafaaf88347d119a4bdd0c6d44abc53/AGENTS.md#L57-L58 sets no pause and no speed-up in battle, along with PlayerLoop/FixedUpdate and the project fixedDeltaTime. Locking an arbitrary fixed rate is prohibited. The current campaign at https://github.com/islee23520/seoul-dengoku/blob/3e3c03349eafaaf88347d119a4bdd0c6d44abc53/GAME/Assets/Janseon/Core/CampaignTurnDomain.cs#L220-L221 advances turns and world ticks. Do not confuse the time-based strategic movement goal of Decision 14 with the current discrete-turn implementation. Product authority: the strategic time cadence is not yet established.

## 9.2 Pulses and Scheduled Commands

CK3 reference: mechanics-01-time-and-pulse.md:11-43,66-181,183-210 covers named on_actions, ID-based distribution of trigger days, AI skipping, and monthly hook distribution. It is not evidence of the overall scheduler execution order. The second/day values at depth-04-war-and-binary.md:1402-1426 are also not Seoul''s time laws. Seoul fact: the code channels examined are ledger TypedEvents and scoped session events (DeterministicCore.cs:111-118,221-225; BattleSessionDriver.cs:25-27). Do not assert the absence of a global bus beyond the scope examined. Product authority: introducing pulses is itself not yet established, and deterministic scheduled commands recorded in the ledger are merely a candidate consistency technique if introduction is decided, not an adopted one.

## 9.3 Micro-to-World Events

Seoul fact: maintain the per-character randomness, cause IDs, and event ledger of save-and-determinism and SP-1.0.0, and distinguish personal life lines from the thresholds of world events. CK3 reference: internal-architecture-synthesis.md:63-76 is a map of local functions and does not prove an end-to-end happens-before chain from daily to monthly to event to save. Product authority: new event thresholds, firing cycles, weights, and performance skips are not yet established.

[Product Decision Ledger — Undecided Items Are Owner Authority](/gdd/design/open-decisions/)

[Korean Orthography and Naming Rules](/gdd/design/korean-terminology-and-naming/)

## Execution Gate for Unconfirmed Integration

Strategic time conversion depends on the open-decision ledger OD-MOVE and product authority. Until the Estate WorldSeconds→world Tick alignment is closed, no integration that assumes production, movement, and activity share a single cycle is finalized. Because CWS1 covers world facts only, no claim is made of complete full-campaign recovery including purpose-specific random numbers, events, and receipts. Save format/version support and lineage recovery boundaries are decision gates under ADR-008, the open-decision ledger OD-SESS, and product authority, and no new migration defaults are invented. This gate is not a new game rule that halts existing implementations; it is a documentation boundary against promoting unconfirmed meanings to completed implementation.');
