INSERT INTO gdd_document (id, category_id, slug, title, summary, status, sort, source_path, body_md) VALUES ('doc.Archify-D05', 'system-design', 'archify-d05', 'D05 Achipai — Full Logic of Production, Construction, Storage, and Repair', '', 'accepted', 73, 'system-design/Archify-D05.md', '# D05 Achipai — Full Logic of Production, Construction, Storage, and Repair

This page shows, as structural diagrams, the machine inputs, validation order, contract calculations, state and conservation boundaries, and error and hold paths of the production, construction, storage, and repair domain. The sources are the relevant mechanism contracts and the 2026-10-08 transition map; numeric approval status follows the source contracts.

## Machine Input and Validation Flow

```archify
{"domainId":"D05","diagramId":"d05-flow","moduleTitle":"D05 Operation Flow"}
```

Consumer contract (conservation-with-optional-admitted-quality-contest): Bottleneck min of required channel ratios; positive denominators; floor only completed batch, retain residual. Quality contest never invents input/output quantity; recipe accounts for atoms.

## Calculation and Output

```text
inclusive-cutoff [bounded-symbolic-contract] verifiedArrival && arrivalAt <= cutoff
material-conservation [bounded-symbolic-contract] unusedAfter + consumedAfter = unusedBefore + consumedBefore; progressAfter = progressBefore on interruption
reservation-limit [bounded-symbolic-contract] sum(reserved same-item atoms) <= verified available same-item atoms
D05-F1 [Candidate · pre-approval] advance=min(each availableInput/inputPerBatch,work/workPerBatch,energy/energyPerBatch,facilityCap,storageCap); completed=floor(carryProgress+advance); progress=carryProgress+advance-completed
D05-F2 [Candidate · pre-approval] consumed+unused conserved on interruption; recipe must account for input atoms in output,workInProgress,waste; storage reservation before output stage

```

The remaining contract leaves of D05 are preserved as a reconciliation ledger linked to the operation flow. Historical reference formulas and undecided values are not placed on operation edges.

## State Fields and Preservation Boundaries

- recipeId/rulesVersion — nonempty string (identity)
- material quantities — nonnegative integer atoms tagged with itemId and unit (item-specific atom)
- work/progress — nonnegative exact rational (recipe-specific work unit)
- rates/power/duration/facility/storage — nullable unit-tagged recipe specification (item/work/power per named clock interval; capacity in item atoms)
- reservedDemand/consumed/unused — nonnegative exact integer (same item atoms)
- resultId/actorId/ownerId/version — identity string / nonnegative version integer (identity / revision)
- arrivalAt/cutoff — finite numeric documentary clock coordinate (same supplied world clock unit)

The data owner is D05 production, stage, and economic-effect settlement; D13 ownership, D02 body state, and D18 time and storage are related; the maintained contracts are inclusive-cutoff, material-conservation, and reservation-limit. The state-ownership boundary covers recipe version,required channels,arrival receipts,available/reserved atoms,consumed,WIP,waste,output,residual,storage reservation. Commit rules: Version-bound owner candidate; current grant/consent/receipt guards; preserve quantities/identities/consumed progress; atomic accepted receipt. Exact source contract referenced below.

## Error and Hold Codes

- Candidate errors: E_POLICY, E_CONSERVATION, E_INPUT, E_UNIT
- Existing evaluator errors: E_TYPE, E_FIELDS, E_INTEGER, E_ID, E_UNKNOWN, E_RATIO, E_FACILITY, E_RESULTS, E_RESERVATION, E_KIND
- Adapter combination rules: tagged unresolved -> Held E_UNRESOLVED; malformed missing required key -> Rejected E_INPUT; stale -> E_REVISION; unit -> E_UNIT; conservation -> E_CONSERVATION. Authority/consent/feasibility privately distinct.

## Removal of Borrowed Formulas and Scope of Application

Borrowed formulas to remove: —. No confirmed GURPS arithmetic in inspected formulaSheet/evaluator; retain ordinary counts, sets, sums and policy locks. D09 reference explicitly invokes no contest.

- BigInt bottleneck min/floor/residual only, required channels selected by caller, no resources/recipe mutation
- Number bottleneck candidate, no exact authoritative conservation

Current scope limit: Named helper only; no complete authoritative domain state owner/transaction/consumer workbook. The next implementation unit is U-D05-recipe-bottleneck-transaction (TOOL/tools/mechanisms/original-trpg/recipe-bottleneck-transaction.mjs, TOOL/tools/mechanisms/original-trpg/recipe-bottleneck-transaction.test.mjs). Separately from the approval of character and world values, this Achipai shows only the contract structure.

## Processing by Flow Node and Original Steps

- Production and work request — receives the recipe, identity, owner, rules, revision, result ID, materials, progress, and approval inputs. (Source: d05.b9.orderedSteps[0])
- Required-value, version, and result check — the source D05 rulesVersion=null is not filled in as a new execution version. Checks the supported version, actor, and existing result ID. (Source: d05.b9.orderedSteps[0]; d05.b9.orderedSteps[1]; d05.b9.orderedSteps[5])
- Input, replay, and conservation conflict — on a rule, revision, actor, reused result, unit, integer, fraction, or resource error, the previous state is kept. (Source: d05.b9.orderedSteps[1]; d05.b9.orderedSteps[4]; d05.b9.orderedSteps[5]; d05.b9.orderedSteps[8])
- Recipe, conversion, and release hold — if the actual recipe, rate, capacity, consumption, recovery, or execution version is undecided, only the dependent transitions are held. This is not a zero-production success. (Source: d05.b9.orderedSteps[1]; d05.b9.orderedSteps[2]; d05.b9.orderedSteps[5]; d05.b9.orderedSteps[6])
- Read approved body state — only reads the D02 state. Checks the approval binding of person/bodyState/bodyRevision/effect. (Source: d05.b9.orderedSteps[2])
- One-time effect settlement key — personId+bodyStateId+bodyRevision+effectId, independent of the economic resultId. The same effect is not deducted repeatedly. (Source: d05.b9.orderedSteps[2])
- No reapplication of existing effects — labor loss that was settled previously is not used again. (Source: d05.b9.orderedSteps[2])
- Approved economic effect candidate — the approved derived effect and the settlement key are prepared in the same candidate. The body ledger is not changed. (Source: d05.b9.orderedSteps[2])
- Atomic recording of effect and key — the settlement key and the actual economic effect are applied together and are retained on load as well. (Source: d05.b9.orderedSteps[2])
- Verified actual arrival — evidence of arrival location, identity, receipt, and rights at the same world time. (Source: d05.b9.orderedSteps[3])
- arrivalAt≤cutoff — included if equal to the deadline. This is time eligibility only; the final stock is separately subject to receipt and rights guards. (Source: d05.b9.orderedSteps[3])
- Excluded from this deadline — late cargo and materials are not deleted, and are not counted as available quantity for the current reservation. (Source: d05.b9.orderedSteps[3])
- Reserve mandatory demand first — mandatory consumption, contracts, and supplies come first from verified stock. Sum of same-item reservations ≤ available atoms. (Source: d05.b9.orderedSteps[3]; d05.b9.orderedSteps[4])
- All constraints of the approved order and recipe — labor, input, power, facility, storage, knowledge, duty, and authority must all be satisfied. An undetermined required channel is held. The proposed bottleneck and yield formulas are not executed. (Source: d05.b9.orderedSteps[5]; d05.b9.orderedSteps[4]; d05.b9.orderedSteps[6])
- Single consumption and fractional progress — only approved work advances, in exact recipe units. Consumed+unused is conserved, and materials are attributed to WIP, waste, or output. (Source: d05.b9.orderedSteps[6]; d05.b9.orderedSteps[7])
- Destination storage reservation — a storage reservation matching the work, stage, and output destination must be secured in the same snapshot. (Source: d05.b9.orderedSteps[7])
- Wait for the previous completed stage — without a reservation, fractional and completed progress, consumption, and unused physical goods are retained. No output, re-consumption, or rollback. (Source: d05.b9.orderedSteps[7])
- Entering the output and storage stage — a reservation permits entry only. It is not an automatic output commit or a numeric recipe approval. (Source: d05.b9.orderedSteps[7]; d05.b9.orderedSteps[8])
- Material and progress conservation check — on interruption, unusedAfter+consumedAfter = the previous sum, and progressAfter=progressBefore. No arbitrary rounding outside completed batches. (Source: d05.b9.orderedSteps[8])
- Atomic application of result and revision — only the verified candidate is applied to the result and revision. (Source: d05.b9.orderedSteps[8])
- Interruption, cancellation, death, occupation, and restoration — lifecycle events that separate progress from ownership. (Source: d05.b9.orderedSteps[6]; d05.b9.orderedSteps[8])
- Retain progress, consumption, and institution ownership — no consumption refund, automatic succession, or transfer of name. Detailed cancellation and death-release policy is held. (Source: d05.b9.orderedSteps[6])
- Restore exact save and reservation — restore the compatible identity, rule, quantity, progress, reservation, and applied IDs, and re-check the save reservation before entering output. (Source: d05.b9.orderedSteps[8]; d05.b9.orderedSteps[1]; d05.b9.orderedSteps[7])
- Recipe, conversion, and release hold — if the actual recipe, rate, capacity, consumption, recovery, or execution version is undecided, only the dependent transitions are held. This is not a zero-production success. (Source: d05.b9.orderedSteps[1]; d05.b9.orderedSteps[2]; d05.b9.orderedSteps[5]; d05.b9.orderedSteps[6])

