INSERT INTO gdd_document (id, category_id, slug, title, summary, status, sort, source_path, body_md) VALUES ('doc.Archify-D06', 'system-design', 'archify-d06', 'D06 Architecture Diagram — Full Logic of Movement, Cargo, Map, and Observation', '', 'accepted', 74, 'system-design/Archify-D06.md', '# D06 Architecture Diagram — Full Logic of Movement, Cargo, Map, and Observation

This page shows, as a structural diagram, the machine inputs, validation order, contract calculations, state and conservation boundaries, and error and hold paths of the movement, cargo, map, and observation domain. The sources are the relevant mechanism contract and the 2026-10-08 transition map; the approval status of numeric values follows the original contract.

## Machine Input and Validation Flow

```archify
{"domainId":"D06","diagramId":"d06-flow","moduleTitle":"D06 Operational Flow"}
```

Consumer contract (conservation-with-optional-observation-contest): Legal actual edge/reach before travel; remaining=before-min(before,traversed). No roll for arrival or cargo. Observation contest may create observer knowledge only. Speed/load policy unresolved; no ST derivation.

## Calculation and Output

```text
basic-lift-reference [public-Lite-derived-structure] BLraw = ST^2 / 5 lb; if BLraw >= 10 lb, round to nearest whole lb for the rounded display value
personal-basic-move-reference [public-Lite-derived-structure] BasicSpeed = (DX + HT) / 4; BasicMove = floor(BasicSpeed)
personal-encumbrance-reference [public-Lite-derived-structure] thresholds = BL*[1,2,3,6,10]; choose the first inclusive threshold containing load; Move = max(1,floor(BasicMove*[1,.8,.6,.4,.2][level]))
route-legality [approved-Seoul-bounded] legal = routeConnected AND passageAuthorized AND segmentPassable
segment-residual [approved-conservation-shape-with-held-rate] remainingAfter = max(0, remainingBefore - traversedDistance); arrived = legal AND remainingAfter = 0
cargo-split-conservation [approved-Seoul-bounded] parentAtoms = disjointUnion(childAtoms); active parent retires; active child quantity sum equals parent quantity
inclusive-cutoff [approved-Seoul-bounded] temporalEligibility = verifiedArrival AND arrivalAt <= cutoffAt
observation-record [approved-Seoul-bounded] knowledge.status = reported; knowledge.observedAt = receiptTime; knowledge.asOf = sourceAsOf; currentWorldFact remains unchanged
reinforcement-arrival-boundary [approved-owner-rule] mayJoin = arrivalVerified AND battleState = ongoing; battleState = ended => false
D06-F1 [Candidate · Pre-Approval] legal=connected && passageAuthorized && passable; remainingAfter=max(0,remaining-traversed); cargo childAtoms disjoint union equals parentAtoms
D06-F2 [Candidate · Pre-Approval] if load<=hardMaximum and legal: speed=v0*routeFactor*availability/(1+load/carryReference); traversed=min(remaining,speed*dt); no strategic squad conversion
D06-F3 [Candidate · Pre-Approval] mayJoin=verifiedActualArrival && battleStatus==ongoing; ended=>false; observation writes observer knowledge not world fact

```

The remaining contract leaves of D06 are preserved as a cross-check ledger linked to the operational flow. Historical reference formulas and unresolved values are not placed on operational edges.

## State Fields and Preservation Boundaries

- routeId/segmentId/moverId/cargoLotId/reportId/resultId — nonempty stable identity string (identity)
- rulesVersion/snapshotVersion — nonempty string / nonnegative safe integer (revision)
- segmentDistance — finite nonnegative number (route-defined distance unit)
- baseMove — positive finite number (yd/s for personal Lite-derived calculation only)
- basicLift/loadWeight — positive/nonnegative finite number (lb)
- encumbranceLevel — integer 0..4 (Lite row index)
- strategicSpeed/fatigueCost/terrainFactor — nullable unit-tagged number (must be issued by a future Seoul movement table)
- remainingDistance/segmentProgress — nonnegative exact rational or finite number (same segment distance unit)
- arrivalAt/cutoffAt/observedAt/asOf — finite number on one named world clock (same D18 clock coordinate)
- verifiedArrival/receiverCountersigned/routeConnected/passageAuthorized/segmentPassable — boolean or null (predicate)
- cargoAtoms — array of unique stable atom identifiers (material identity)
- knowledgeRecord — subjectId, sourceId, observedAt, asOf and status (identity + clock + enum)

The data owner is D06 movement, cargo transport, and observation knowledge; D13 rights and custody, D18 time and storage. The maintained contracts are route-legality, segment-residual, cargo-split-conservation, inclusive-cutoff, observation-record, and reinforcement-arrival-boundary. The state ownership boundaries are actual route edge,access/passability,remaining distance,cargo atom partition,arrival receipt,observer knowledge snapshot. Commit rules: Version-bound owner candidate; current grant/consent/receipt guards; preserve quantities/identities/consumed progress; atomic accepted receipt. Exact source contract referenced below.

## Error and Hold Codes

- Candidate errors: E_AUTHORITY, E_POLICY, E_UNIT, E_EXTERNAL_ORDER
- Existing evaluator errors: E_TYPE, E_RANGE, E_DUPLICATE_ID, E_OVER_CAPACITY, E_NO_PATH, E_ROUTE_AUTHORITY, E_SEGMENT_BLOCKED, E_PROPOSAL_REQUIRED, E_ZERO_SPEED, E_CONSERVATION
- Adapter combination rules: tagged unresolved -> Held E_UNRESOLVED; malformed missing required key -> Rejected E_INPUT; stale -> E_REVISION; unit -> E_UNIT; conservation -> E_CONSERVATION. Authority/consent/feasibility privately distinct.

## Removal of Borrowed Formulas and Scope of Application

Borrowed formulas to be removed: basic-lift-reference, personal-basic-move-reference, personal-encumbrance-reference. Remove call/dependency from original operative consumer, not original records/historical references/tests.

- pure safe integer margin/outcome and caller-authorized projection, no profile/rating/receipt authority
- caller-supplied trusted boolean gates only; no provenance/authentication/world resolver, absent tag unsupported

Current scope limits: Named helper only; no complete authoritative domain state owner/transaction/consumer workbook. The next implementation unit is U-D06-legal-travel-observation(TOOL/tools/mechanisms/original-trpg/legal-travel-observation.mjs, TOOL/tools/mechanisms/original-trpg/legal-travel-observation.test.mjs). Separately from the approval of character and world values, this diagram shows only the contract structure.

## Processing by Flow Node and Original Steps

- Movement, cargo, and report request — exact route, segment, traveler, cargo, observation, time, rule, and snapshot IDs. (Source: d06.b9.orderedSteps[0])
- Version, unit, atom, and replay check — reject changed result IDs, stale data, mixed rules, duplicate cargo atoms, and unit errors. Exactly supported replay has no additional effect. (Source: d06.b9.orderedSteps[0]; d06.b9.orderedSteps[1])
- Independent operation types — movement, split, arrival, report, and reinforcement are separate operations and are not tied together in a sequential chain. (Source: d06.b9.orderedSteps[1]; d06.b9.orderedSteps[2]; d06.b9.orderedSteps[5]; d06.b9.orderedSteps[6]; d06.b9.orderedSteps[8]; d06.b9.orderedSteps[9])
- Reject mismatches and impossibilities — format, revision, unit, atom, illegal path, and timestamp errors. Keep the previous state. (Source: d06.b9.orderedSteps[1]; d06.b9.orderedSteps[2]; d06.b9.orderedSteps[4]; d06.b9.orderedSteps[5]; d06.b9.orderedSteps[7]; d06.b9.orderedSteps[8])
- Pending input, speed, and causality — unknown paths, the actual strategic speed table, effect policy, and the order of simultaneous war endings are undecided and held back. (Source: d06.b9.orderedSteps[2]; d06.b9.orderedSteps[3]; d06.b9.orderedSteps[6]; d06.b9.orderedSteps[7]; d06.b9.orderedSteps[9])
- Connected, passable, and traversable — all three are currently true. Map lines, same-name facilities, and surface adjacency are not edges or permissions. (Source: d06.b9.orderedSteps[2]; d06.b9.orderedSteps[4]; d06.b9.orderedSteps[3])
- Segment blockage and replanning — keep the completed distance and current position, and stop further movement. No arbitrary detours or teleport. (Source: d06.b9.orderedSteps[4])
- Approved movement amount and unit check — personal Lite Move/BL is a historical reference only and not a strategic coefficient. An approved external traversedDistance and a positive speed are required. (Source: d06.b9.orderedSteps[3]; d06.b9.orderedSteps[4])
- Remaining segment calculation — remainingAfter=max(0,remainingBefore-traversedDistance). If it is 0 on a legal segment, the unit has arrived. Surplus must not be carried over automatically to the next segment. (Source: d06.b9.orderedSteps[4])
- Position and progress candidate — record only the segments actually traversed and the completed distance. (Source: d06.b9.orderedSteps[4]; d06.b9.orderedSteps[10])
- Atom-complete, disjoint split — the disjoint union of childAtoms = parentAtoms. Matching names or quantities alone is not enough. (Source: d06.b9.orderedSteps[5])
- Parent retired, children active — after a complete split, only the parent is retired. Separation of title, custody, and provenance is preserved. (Source: d06.b9.orderedSteps[5]; d06.b9.orderedSteps[10])
- Actual arrival identity and position — arrival verification takes precedence over reservation, production, and consumption at the same timestamp. (Source: d06.b9.orderedSteps[6])
- Inclusive cutoff comparison — verifiedArrival AND arrivalAt≤cutoff. When they are equal, time eligibility holds. (Source: d06.b9.orderedSteps[6]; d06.b9.orderedSteps[7])
- Excluded from this cutoff only — the cargo exists and is left for later application processing. (Source: d06.b9.orderedSteps[6]; d06.b9.orderedSteps[10])
- Receiver confirmation and rights — receiverCountersigned and a separately approved custody/rights condition are required. The unapproved strengthened formula custodian AND receiver is forbidden. (Source: d06.b9.orderedSteps[7])
- Available stock candidate — time eligibility alone does not issue stock; reflection in the owning domain is required. (Source: d06.b9.orderedSteps[7]; d06.b9.orderedSteps[10])
- Source, observation, and reference-time check — subject/source/observedAt/sourceAsOf are required. It is an error if the reference time is later than the acquisition time. (Source: d06.b9.orderedSteps[8])
- Update observer knowledge only — status=report, observedAt=receiptTime, asOf=sourceAsOf. Current world facts are unchanged. There is no universal TTL. (Source: d06.b9.orderedSteps[8]; d06.b9.orderedSteps[10])
- Actual arrival and current combat state — verifiedActualArrival and whether the battle is ongoing. Origin, rank, initial roster, capacity, and arbitrary arrival windows are forbidden. (Source: d06.b9.orderedSteps[9])
- Joining an ongoing battle is possible — entry eligibility is separate from command transfer and capacity. (Source: d06.b9.orderedSteps[9]; d06.b9.orderedSteps[10])
- Joining a finished battle is not possible — the arrival fact is kept, but the unit does not retroactively join the ended encounter. (Source: d06.b9.orderedSteps[9]; d06.b9.orderedSteps[10])
- Single application of results and revisions — only per-branch candidates are preserved, and they are applied once after the revision check. (Source: d06.b9.orderedSteps[10])
- Cancellation, death, and restoration — completed movement, consumption, cargo, and report history are preserved. (Source: d06.b9.orderedSteps[10])
- Preserve progress, cargo, and knowledge — restore the exact segment, remainder, cargo provenance, knowledge timestamp, result ID, and version. Death does not delete position or cargo. (Source: d06.b9.orderedSteps[10]; d06.b9.orderedSteps[1])

