| Operation — Family and Property Procedure Requests | d08.b9.orderedSteps[0] | "Read stable action, result, participant, forum-law, rules-version and snapshot identities." |
| Operation — Uniqueness of IDs, Revisions, and Records | d08.b9.orderedSteps[1] | "Reject malformed IDs, duplicate attributed records, stale snapshot, incompatible rules version or changed duplicate result before mutation." |
| Operation — Independent Family Work | d08.b9.orderedSteps[2] | "Resolve the explicitly registered forum law. Unknown registration, authority or route permission yields unresolved; never select a party''s country by fallback." |
| Operation — Registration Jurisdiction, Authority, and Path | d08.b9.orderedSteps[3] | "Record each direct participant consent and each ratification as separate attributed facts. A record never substitutes for another record." |
| Operation — Separate Records of Consent and Ratification | d08.b9.orderedSteps[4] | "For marriage, ask the registered forum adjudicator for an attributed formation result. Without it, preserve records and return undetermined-law or records-present as applicable." |
| Operation — Marriage Formation | d08.b9.orderedSteps[5] | "If formation is confirmed, write zero new claims and zero territory transfers for marriage formation itself while preserving existing rights and other claim routes." |
| Operation — Death, Detention, and Loss of Office | d08.b9.orderedSteps[6] | "On death, detention or office loss, evaluate alliance, property, ratification and heir effects independently through their owning contracts. Unknown outcomes remain undetermined and no bulk close occurs." |
| Operation — Separation of Alliance, Property, Ratification, and Succession | d08.b9.orderedSteps[7] | "On living office loss, stop only that office''s signature, command and operation. Do not dissolve marriage, appoint an heir, transfer property or absorb authority." |
| Operation — Independent Family Work | d08.b9.orderedSteps[8] | "For joint property, compare the exact signer set with the exact current-owner set; if equal, emit only a D13 contract-eligible receipt, not a title transfer." |
| Operation — Registration Jurisdiction, Authority, and Path | d08.b9.orderedSteps[9] | "For adoption, require named participant consents, then require an approved registered procedure. Without the procedure, preserve records and return undetermined-procedure."​ |
| Operation — Independent Family Work | d08.b9.orderedSteps[10] | "Reject any attempt to list a recognized synthetic person as transferable property." |
| Operation — Record Only, Explicitly Not Formed | d08.b9.orderedSteps[11] | "Commit one result, record and revision atomically. Failed or unresolved operations preserve the prior world state except for explicitly allowed record-only writes." |
