| Operation — Office, Procedure, and Acting-Authority Requests | d09.b9.orderedSteps[0] | "Resolve stable IDs, exact rules version, state, institution, office and procedure revision; reject any mismatch or duplicate event." |
| Operation — Office Event Types | d09.b9.orderedSteps[1] | "For office loss or holder death supplied by the owning lifecycle event, clear only the target office; preserve institution, treasury and unrelated offices; emit selection-pending; generate no replacement." |
| Operation — Office Event Types | d09.b9.orderedSteps[2] | "For a procedure attempt, require approvalStatus=approved and every field required by that state/office selector. Proposal or missing payload returns E_PROPOSAL with the full before state unchanged." |
| Operation — Approved State and Office Procedure | d09.b9.orderedSteps[3] | "Filter candidate records by explicit eligible=true. If the selector requires an examination, require declared score unit and retain candidates whose score is at least the registered threshold. No candidate leaves a vacancy with no-candidate status." |
| Operation — Empty Candidate Set | d09.b9.orderedSteps[4] | "For vote selectors, validate unique eligible voters and unique ballots, then test the registered quorum exactly. Unmet quorum leaves the vacancy and records quorum-unmet." |
| Operation — Registered Quorum | d09.b9.orderedSteps[5] | "Count one valid ballot per eligible voter. Select the unique highest tally. On a top tie, apply only the registered tie rule: exact resolver order selects the first tied ID present; remain-vacant records tie-unresolved." |
| Operation — Voting and Appointment Paths | d09.b9.orderedSteps[6] | "For appointment selectors, require the registered appointing actor. For every selector, require the registered ratifier only when ratificationRequired=tru​e. A missing or wrong actor leaves the office unchanged and fails explicitly." |
| Operation — Appointer and Required Ratifier | d09.b9.orderedSteps[7] | "Commit holder/effective/vacant and categorical legitimacy together. Preserve treasury and institution fields byte-for-byte; record no numeric legitimacy value." |
| Operation — Office Event Types | d09.b9.orderedSteps[8] | "For an acting request, require an exact actor and action listed in actingRule. Set only the scoped acting receipt; never fill the office or grant unlisted actions." |
| Operation — Applying Target Results and Receipts | d09.b9.orderedSteps[9] | "On load, restore receipts and revisions without rerunning selection. On cancel/death during an uncommitted attempt, keep the vacancy and discard no prior institution or treasury history." |
