- Hold and Preserve Original State — Only the dependent action is put on hold because of unconfirmed or unapproved input. The world does not stop, and consumption and completion progress are preserved. (Source: see the domain contract flow and detail items)
- Explicit Error and Preserve Original State — Errors in format, unit, edition, authority, consent, feasibility, and preservation are explicitly rejected. No new state, reservation, random number, or acceptance receipt is applied. (Source: see the domain contract flow and detail items)
- Replay Stored Result — The same acceptance identity and same content from a general adapter returns the existing result. There are no additional effects, random number consumption, or revisions. Existing per-evaluator duplicate errors are not arbitrarily removed. (Source: see the domain contract flow and detail items)
- Atomic Verification of Selection Results — After verifying preservation of the identity, quantity, authority, and completion consumption that the action permitted, atomically apply the result, revision, and receipt. (Source: d15.b9.writeSet[0]; d15.b9.writeSet[1]; d15.b9.writeSet[2]; d15.b9.writeSet[4]; d15.b9.writeSet[5])
- Return Result and Permitted Projection — Returns the recorded result of the action or a read-only result. Does not display hidden facts beyond the observer''s knowledge and access rights, nor claim that implementation is complete. (Source: see the domain contract flow and detail items)
- Maintain Existing State — Unconfirmed previews, non-binding proposals, and explicit refusals leave the existing state unchanged. Completed consumption and progress are not rolled back. (Source: see the domain contract flow and detail items)

