| Operation — Current Edition and Action Selection | d18.b11.sourceClaims[1].​rule | "Permanent IDs resolve entity and event identity, and revision conflicts are explicit rather than silently renumbered, migrated or mixed." |
| Historical Reference — Excluded from Operational Path | d18.b11.sourceClaims[1].​sources[0] | "SP-1.0.0 sp1.b12-sp1.b13" |
| Historical Reference — Excluded from Operational Path | d18.b11.sourceClaims[1].​sources[1] | "SP-1.0.0 sp1.b93 and sp1.b107-sp1.b109" |
| Historical Reference — Excluded from Operational Path | d18.b11.sourceClaims[1].​sources[2] | "scope-map /decisions/14" |
| Historical Reference — Excluded from Operational Path | d18.b11.sourceClaims[2].​id | "battle-control" |
| Operation — Current Edition and Action Selection | d18.b11.sourceClaims[2].​rule | "The body commander directly commands every assigned squad inside the registered command scope, but not enemies, unassigned independents or out-of-scope allies." |
| Historical Reference — Excluded from Operational Path | d18.b11.sourceClaims[2].​sources[0] | "SP-1.0.0 sp1.b111" |
| Historical Reference — Excluded from Operational Path | d18.b11.sourceClaims[2].​sources[1] | "scope-map /decisions/8" |
| Historical Reference — Excluded from Operational Path | d18.b11.sourceClaims[3].​id | "immediate-orders-autono​my-evaluation" |
| Operation — Current Edition and Action Selection | d18.b11.sourceClaims[3].​rule | "Battle orders arrive immediately; the body squad leader may comply, partially comply or act independently. After actual execution results, appraisal belongs to the original issuing commander person and becomes that person’s memory and later assignment/trust evidence. Compliance and performance remain separate, with original sender, command and result identity preserved; subordinate autonomy does not transfer appraisal ownership." |
| Historical Reference — Excluded from Operational Path | d18.b11.sourceClaims[3].​sources[0] | "SP-1.0.0 sp1.b112-sp1.b115" |
| Historical Reference — Excluded from Operational Path | d18.b11.sourceClaims[3].​sources[1] | "scope-map /decisions/9" |
| Historical Reference — Excluded from Operational Path | d18.b11.sourceClaims[4].​id | "realtime-no-control-too​ls" |
| Operation — Current Edition and Action Selection | d18.b11.sourceClaims[4].​rule | "Battle supports real-time unit commands but no pause, speed control or order queue." |
| Historical Reference — Excluded from Operational Path | d18.b11.sourceClaims[4].​sources[0] | "SP-1.0.0 sp1.b92" |
| Historical Reference — Excluded from Operational Path | d18.b11.sourceClaims[4].​sources[1] | "SP-1.0.0 sp1.b108" |
| Historical Reference — Excluded from Operational Path | d18.b11.sourceClaims[4].​sources[2] | "scope-map /decisions/10" |
| Historical Reference — Excluded from Operational Path | d18.b11.sourceClaims[5].​id | "any-actual-arrival-rein​forces" |
| Operation — Current Edition and Action Selection | d18.b11.sourceClaims[5].​rule | "Any unit that actually arrives while battle is ongoing may participate as reinforcement; no origin, rank, initial-roster or invented time-window gate is added." |
| Historical Reference — Excluded from Operational Path | d18.b11.sourceClaims[5].​sources[0] | "OWNER-REINFORCEMENT-202​61004" |
| Historical Reference — Excluded from Operational Path | d18.b11.sourceClaims[5].​sources[1] | "scope-map /decisions/15" |
| Historical Reference — Excluded from Operational Path | d18.b11.sourceClaims[6].​id | "valid-cb-and-custom-neg​otiation" |
| Operation — Current Edition and Action Selection | d18.b11.sourceClaims[6].​rule | "War requires a valid registered casus belli with a named eligible beneficiary fixed to it at opening; holding a claim alone grants neither declaration authority nor forces. Below absolute war score 100, both sides may negotiate itemized terms; unregistered prices block signing and value less than or equal to war score does not auto-accept." |
| Historical Reference — Excluded from Operational Path | d18.b11.sourceClaims[6].​sources[0] | "SP-1.0.0 sp1.b117-sp1.b119" |
| Historical Reference — Excluded from Operational Path | d18.b11.sourceClaims[6].​sources[1] | "SP-1.0.0 sp1.b122-sp1.b126" |
| Historical Reference — Excluded from Operational Path | d18.b11.sourceClaims[6].​sources[2] | "scope-map /decisions/11" |
| Historical Reference — Excluded from Operational Path | d18.b11.sourceClaims[6].​sources[3] | "scope-map /decisions/13" |
| Historical Reference — Excluded from Operational Path | d18.b11.sourceClaims[7].​id | "forced-goal-limited-end​points" |
| Operation — Current Edition and Action Selection | d18.b11.sourceClaims[7].​rule | "At exact war score +100 or -100, re-read the opening casus-belli revision and fixed beneficiary, and recheck continuing grounds and beneficiary eligibility before endpoint effects. A still-valid casus belli terminates immediately by its goal-limited effects; an invalid one follows its registered invalidation rule and creates no unsupported right. Response delay cannot postpone termination or accumulate demands; out-of-goal forced transfer is forbidden." |
